 "comment": "party_monthly attribution and Trial Balance wording (written at the reference's 3b55a03f, true at da9e2d3d). Parties: a supplier paid with bank charges, and a scrap sale by journal with the customer on the same side, are not attributed (indirect expenses, sales); a journal with one party on each side is the other-side party's (Supp Y); a journal with two parties on the other side is several parties; a party netting to nil on a payment (no party on the other side), and a journal whose block lines net to nil (nil), are not attributed; a receipt net of bank charges is not attributed (the money reason: bank on the charges' side), where at 3b55a03f it was the customer's; a round-off on a sales, purchase, credit note and debit note voucher is that voucher's party's though on the same side. The Trial Balance: matched by the optional vouchers alone with cancelled ones also tried (sales); two statuses tried and none of the sets matches (purchases); the one status tried does not match, and a post-dated voucher netting to nil here is no set (direct expenses); the optional vouchers match exactly and are named, and all three statuses together are 30 paise off, which at 3b55a03f also matched (within a rupee) so that both were listed and none chosen (indirect expenses).",
